(window.RW_DISPLAY = window.RW_DISPLAY || {})["test10_2B"] = [{"id":"40270820","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"Catherine L. Cardel ús is a researcher who studies canopy soil. Canopy soil is formed in a tree’s branches (its canopy) when dead leaves and other falling things collect. This material breaks down, becoming canopy soil. Canopy soil helps preserve a healthy water cycle (how water moves through the environment) in rainforests. This benefit is one reason Cardel ús is interested in the canopy soils in large choibá trees in rainforests in Costa Rica.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Catherine L. Cardelús is a researcher who studies canopy soil. Canopy soil is formed in a tree’s branches (its canopy) when dead leaves and","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"other falling things collect. This material breaks down, becoming canopy soil. Canopy soil helps preserve a healthy water cycle (how water","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"moves through the environment) in rainforests. This benefit is one reason Cardelús is interested in the canopy soils in large choibá trees in","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"rainforests in Costa Rica.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best describes the text’s overall structure?","choices":["It explains a disagreement between researchers and how it was resolved.","It presents an idea and mentions a researcher who disagrees with that idea.","It compares the sizes of two types of trees over several years.","It introduces a researcher and gives information about what she researches."]},{"id":"afd48140","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in Context","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Craft and Structure · Words in Context","passage":"In 1877, 85% of California’s railways were already controlled by the Southern Pacific Railroad. The company further solidified its ______ in rail access to the state’s Pacific coast when it completed the Sunset Route in 1883: running from Louisiana to Southern California, the route established the first transcontinental rail line across the southern United States.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"In 1877, 85% of California’s railways were already controlled by the Southern Pacific Railroad. The company further solidified its ______ in rail","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"access to the state’s Pacific coast when it completed the Sunset Route in 1883: running from Louisiana to Southern California, the route","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"established the first transcontinental rail line across the southern United States.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["dominance","creativity","insignificance","neutrality"]},{"id":"6cf906fc","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in Context","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Craft and Structure · Words in Context","passage":"The following text is adapted from José Martí s 1891 poem “At the Salon” (translated by Cecil Charles in 1898). The speaker describes a painting featuring a female figure. From the sterile soil no ray Of hope in a blade of green, Nor sheltering roof is seen — Though the skies are heavy and gray. Ah, this is the woman fair Who stole away my heart In the splendid halls of art Yester-e en as I wandered there! As used in the text,","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The following text is adapted from José Martí’s 1891 poem “At the Salon” (translated by Cecil Charles in 1898). The speaker describes a painting","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"featuring a female figure.","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"From the sterile soil no ray","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Of hope in a blade of green,","indent":3},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Nor sheltering roof is seen—","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Though the skies are heavy and gray.","indent":3},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Ah, this is the woman fair","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Who stole away my heart","indent":3},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"In the splendid halls of art","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Yester-e’en as I wandered there!","indent":3}],"question":"As used in the text, what does the word “sheltering” most nearly mean?","choices":["Protective","Restrictive","Affectionate","Suspicious"],"underline":"sheltering","underline_segments":["sheltering"]},{"id":"571cf537","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in Context","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Craft and Structure · Words in Context","passage":"The author’s claim about the relationship between Neanderthals and Homo sapiens is ______, as it fails to account for several recent archaeological discoveries. To be convincing, his argument would need to address recent finds of additional hominid fossils, such as the latest Denisovan specimens and Homo longi.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The author’s claim about the relationship between Neanderthals and Homo sapiens is ______, as it fails to account for several recent","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"archaeological discoveries. To be convincing, his argument would need to address recent finds of additional hominid fossils, such as the latest","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Denisovan specimens and Homo longi.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["disorienting","tenuous","nuanced","unoriginal"]},{"id":"805e361d","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"Companies are providing consumers with more opportunities to purchase customized products than ever before. Whether buying customized sneakers, jewelry, or clothing, consumers can participate in the design of products to meet their specific needs and tastes. In turn, companies profit too: studies have shown that consumers are willing to pay more and wait longer for a customized product. Still, it can be difficult for companies to offer customization while keeping costs low, as the standard methods of mass production may not be able to accommodate making a unique product each time.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Companies are providing consumers with more opportunities to purchase customized products than ever before. Whether buying customized","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"sneakers, jewelry, or clothing, consumers can participate in the design of products to meet their specific needs and tastes. In turn, companies","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"profit too: studies have shown that consumers are willing to pay more and wait longer for a customized product. Still, it can be difficult for","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"companies to offer customization while keeping costs low, as the standard methods of mass production may not be able to accommodate","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"making a unique product each time.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?","choices":["It discusses several recent innovations in product manufacturing and then suggests some potential applications of those innovations.","It describes a company’s recent success with new products and then explains multiple factors that may have contributed to that success.","It introduces a trend in consumer products and then explains how the trend both benefits and poses a challenge to companies.","It presents two contrasting product-marketing techniques and then provides examples of one of those techniques."]},{"id":"8a47383f","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in Context","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Craft and Structure · Words in Context","passage":"The National Heritage Fellowship was created to publicly ______ exceptional folk and traditional artists in the United States. In 2015, the fellowship was given to the circus aerialist (mid-air acrobat) Dolly Jacobs to celebrate her lifetime contributions to the arts.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The National Heritage Fellowship was created to publicly ______ exceptional folk and traditional artists in the United States. In 2015, the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"fellowship was given to the circus aerialist (mid-air acrobat) Dolly Jacobs to celebrate her lifetime contributions to the arts.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["startle","recognize","familiarize","convey"]},{"id":"0a04cac5","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"The following text is adapted from Jane Austen’s 1814 novel Mansfield Park. The speaker, Tom, is considering staging a play at home with a group of his friends and family. We mean nothing but a little amusement among ourselves, just to vary the scene, and exercise our powers in something new. We want no audience, no publicity. We may be trusted, I think, in choosing some play most perfectly unexceptionable; and I can conceive no greater harm or danger to any of us in conversing in the elegant written language of some respectable author than in chattering in words of our own.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The following text is adapted from Jane Austen’s 1814 novel Mansfield Park. The speaker, Tom, is considering staging a play at home with a","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"group of his friends and family.","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"We mean nothing but a little amusement among ourselves, just to vary the scene, and exercise our powers in something new. We want no","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"audience, no publicity. We may be trusted, I think, in choosing some play most perfectly unexceptionable; and I can conceive no greater harm","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"or danger to any of us in conversing in the elegant written language of some respectable author than in chattering in words of our own.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?","choices":["To offer Tom’s assurance that the play will be inoffensive and involve only a small number of people","To clarify that the play will not be performed in the manner Tom had originally intended","To elaborate on the idea that the people around Tom lack the skills to successfully stage a play","To assert that Tom believes the group performing the play will be able to successfully promote it"]},{"id":"359b891c","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in Context","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Craft and Structure · Words in Context","passage":"Painter Alma W. Thomas was fascinated by the colors and shapes found in nature. The flowers and trees in the garden at her home in Washington, DC, ______ her work. For example, Thomas’s use of broken brushstrokes was inspired by the way that light would shine through the leaves of a tree in front of her house.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Painter Alma W. Thomas was fascinated by the colors and shapes found in nature. The flowers and trees in the garden at her home in","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Washington, DC, ______ her work. For example, Thomas’s use of broken brushstrokes was inspired by the way that light would shine through the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"leaves of a tree in front of her house.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["restricted","announced","distracted","influenced"]},{"id":"96d1c1fe","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Inferences","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Information and Ideas · Inferences","passage":"Tatiana R. Feuerborn and colleagues analyzed the genomes of more than a hundred domesticated dogs from sites in Siberia dating from 11,000 years ago to the present. They found that the dogs constituted a genetically isolated population of Arctic breeds until approximately 2,000 years ago, at which point there was substantial interbreeding with Near Eastern dog breeds. Furthermore, beginning around 2,000 years ago, some sites contain artifacts consistent with a Near East origin, like glass beads, but the people show no evidence of having traveled extensively outside Siberia. From this, Feuerborn and colleagues concluded that around 2,000 years ago ______","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Tatiana R. Feuerborn and colleagues analyzed the genomes of more than a hundred domesticated dogs from sites in Siberia dating from 11,000","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"years ago to the present. They found that the dogs constituted a genetically isolated population of Arctic breeds until approximately 2,000 years","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"ago, at which point there was substantial interbreeding with Near Eastern dog breeds. Furthermore, beginning around 2,000 years ago, some","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"sites contain artifacts consistent with a Near East origin, like glass beads, but the people show no evidence of having traveled extensively","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"outside Siberia. From this, Feuerborn and colleagues concluded that around 2,000 years ago ______","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice most logically completes the text?","choices":["dogs and artifacts like glass beads began to be transported from the Near East to Siberia.","people from Siberia began to reach the Near East, where they acquired dogs and artifacts such as glass beads.","glass beads and other artifacts from the Near East began to be exchanged for dogs from Siberia.","dogs from the Near East began to be exchanged for glass beads and other artifacts from Siberia."]},{"id":"d2c2a7ef","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Information and Ideas · Central Ideas and Details","passage":"The following text is from Anton Chekhov’s 1898 short story “Ionitch” (translated by Marian Fell in 1915). The text is set in a Russian city referred to as the city of S. If newcomers to the little provincial city of S. complained that life there was monotonous and dull, its inhabitants would answer that, on the contrary, S. was a very amusing place, indeed, that it had a library and a club, that balls were given there, and finally, that very pleasant families lived there with whom one might become acquainted. And they always pointed to the Turkins as the most accomplished and most enlightened family of all.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The following text is from Anton Chekhov’s 1898 short story “Ionitch” (translated by Marian Fell in 1915). The text is set in a Russian city referred","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"to as the city of S.","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"If newcomers to the little provincial city of S. complained that life there was monotonous and dull, its inhabitants would answer","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"that, on the contrary, S. was a very amusing place, indeed, that it had a library and a club, that balls were given there, and finally,","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"that very pleasant families lived there with whom one might become acquainted. And they always pointed to the Turkins as the","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"most accomplished and most enlightened family of all.","indent":2}],"question":"What does the text suggest about the Turkins?","choices":["They are relative newcomers to the city of S.","They have a unique status in the city of S.","They have long disliked living in the city of S.","They are amused by the other residents of the city of S."]},{"id":"e946a32e","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"Boldly mixing elements of poetry, fiction, drama, philosophy, and manifesto, Puerto Rican writer Giannina Braschi creates cross-genre literature that explores themes such as immigration and independence. Her works have inspired responses from individuals across different fields and in a wide range of formats, from musical compositions and a comic book to architecture and furniture design. In an essay, a student asserts that the production of these diverse creations by others is reflective of Braschi’s own approach to crafting literature. Which quotation from a scholarly review of Braschi’s work best supports","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Boldly mixing elements of poetry, fiction, drama, philosophy, and manifesto, Puerto Rican writer Giannina Braschi creates cross-genre literature","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"that explores themes such as immigration and independence. Her works have inspired responses from individuals across different fields and in","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"a wide range of formats, from musical compositions and a comic book to architecture and furniture design. In an essay, a student asserts that","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"the production of these diverse creations by others is reflective of Braschi’s own approach to crafting literature.","indent":0}],"question":"Which quotation from a literary critic would best support the student’s claim?","choices":["“Braschi is the focus of a 2020 collection of essays in which fifteen scholars from seven different countries delved into the linguistic and structural patterns of her writings.”","“Braschi’s eagerness to push boundaries and blend genres within literature invites us to consider how other art forms might also engage with literature.”","“Before settling in New York City, where she would go on to become a college professor, Braschi studied both literature and philosophy in several cities around the world.”","“In addition to her creative literary works, Braschi has produced academic pieces analyzing writings by Miguel de Cervantes, Federico García Lorca, and other authors.”"]},{"id":"df654a2b","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Inferences","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Information and Ideas · Inferences","passage":"Zines are small-scale, self-printed magazines. They have been around since the Black literary zine Fire!! was created in the 1920s. Since then, zines have appealed to creators looking for an inexpensive form of expression to share with a select audience. Zine creators often mix art with social commentary and challenge mainstream culture. At first, the internet appeared to replace the zine, but this old form persists. Today, there are enough zines in the United States to support annual zine festivals. This suggests that ______","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Zines are small-scale, self-printed magazines. They have been around since the Black literary zine Fire!! was created in the 1920s. Since then,","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"zines have appealed to creators looking for an inexpensive form of expression to share with a select audience. Zine creators often mix art with","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"social commentary and challenge mainstream culture. At first, the internet appeared to replace the zine, but this old form persists. Today, there","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"are enough zines in the United States to support annual zine festivals. This suggests that ______","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice most logically completes the text?","choices":["creators can reach a larger audience by posting online.","zines are still a meaningful form of expression.","creators can continue to explore new art forms.","zines are good sources of mainstream culture."]},{"id":"ac285054","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Inferences","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Information and Ideas · Inferences","passage":"The domestic sweet potato (Ipomoea batatas) descends from a wild plant native to South America. It also populates the Polynesian Islands, where evidence confirms that Native Hawaiians and other Indigenous peoples were cultivating the plant centuries before seafaring first occurred over the thousands of miles of ocean separating them from South America. To explain how the sweet potato was first introduced in Polynesia, botanist Pablo Muñoz-Rodríguez and colleagues analyzed the DNA of numerous varieties of the plant, concluding that Polynesian varieties diverged from South American ones over 100,000 years ago. Given that Polynesia was peopled only in the last three thousand years, the team concluded that ______","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The domestic sweet potato (Ipomoea batatas) descends from a wild plant native to South America. It also populates the Polynesian Islands,","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"where evidence confirms that Native Hawaiians and other Indigenous peoples were cultivating the plant centuries before seafaring first occurred","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"over the thousands of miles of ocean separating them from South America. To explain how the sweet potato was first introduced in Polynesia,","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"botanist Pablo Muñoz-Rodríguez and colleagues analyzed the DNA of numerous varieties of the plant, concluding that Polynesian varieties","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"diverged from South American ones over 100,000 years ago. Given that Polynesia was peopled only in the last three thousand years, the team","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"concluded that ______","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice most logically completes the text?","choices":["the cultivation of the sweet potato in Polynesia likely predates its cultivation in South America.","Polynesian peoples likely acquired the sweet potato from South American peoples only within the last three thousand years.","human activity likely played no role in the introduction of the sweet potato in Polynesia.","Polynesian sweet potato varieties likely descend from a single South American variety that was domesticated, not wild."]},{"id":"3d91c973","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"Mosasaurs were large marine reptiles that lived in the Late Cretaceous period, approximately 100 million to 66 million years ago. Celina Suarez, Alberto Pérez-Huerta, and T. Lynn Harrell Jr. examined oxygen-18 isotopes in mosasaur tooth enamel","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Mosasaurs were large marine reptiles that lived in the Late Cretaceous period, approximately 100 million to 66 million years ago. Celina Suarez,","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Alberto Pérez-Huerta, and T. Lynn Harrell Jr. examined oxygen-18 isotopes in mosasaur tooth enamel in order to calculate likely mosasaur body","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"temperatures and determined that mosasaurs were endothermic—that is, they used internal metabolic processes to maintain a stable body","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"temperature in a variety of ambient temperatures. Suarez, Pérez-Huerta, and Harrell claim that endothermy would have enabled mosasaurs to","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"include relatively cold polar waters in their range.","indent":0}],"question":"Which finding, if true, would most directly support Suarez, Pérez-Huerta, and Harrell’s claim?","choices":["Mosasaurs likely body temperatures are easier to determine from tooth enamel oxygen-18 isotope data than the body temperatures of nonendothermic Late Cretaceous marine reptiles are.","Fossils of both mosasaurs and nonendothermic marine reptiles have been found in roughly equal numbers in regions known to be near the poles during the Late Cretaceous, though in lower concentrations than elsewhere.","Several mosasaur fossils have been found in regions known to be near the poles during the Late Cretaceous, while relatively few fossils of nonendothermic marine reptiles have been found in those locations.","During the Late Cretaceous, seawater temperatures were likely higher throughout mosasaurs range, including near the poles, than seawater temperatures at those same latitudes are today."]},{"id":"d76ea360","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"Puerto Rico is an island in the Caribbean Sea. Indigenous people there started raising guinea pigs about 1,700 years ago. Guinea pigs had originally been domesticated much earlier in both Colombia and Peru. So were guinea pigs brought to Puerto Rico from Colombia or from Peru? Ancient Caribbean trade routes connected Puerto Rico with Colombia but not with Peru. Therefore, guinea pigs in Puerto Rico probably came from Colombia and descended from Colombian guinea pigs.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Puerto Rico is an island in the Caribbean Sea. Indigenous people there started raising guinea pigs about 1,700 years ago. Guinea pigs had","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"originally been domesticated much earlier in both Colombia and Peru. So were guinea pigs brought to Puerto Rico from Colombia or from Peru?","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Ancient Caribbean trade routes connected Puerto Rico with Colombia but not with Peru. Therefore, guinea pigs in Puerto Rico probably came","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"from Colombia and descended from Colombian guinea pigs.","indent":0}],"question":"Which finding, if true, would most directly weaken the underlined claim?","choices":["Ancient guinea pigs in Puerto Rico were genetically less similar to ancient guinea pigs in Colombia than to ancient guinea pigs in Peru.","Guinea pigs are common in ancient Puerto Rican art, especially in pottery.","Modern breeds of guinea pigs don’t look like images of guinea pigs in ancient art from Puerto Rico, Colombia, and Peru.","The guinea pig population of ancient Colombia was much larger than the guinea pig population of ancient Peru."],"underline":null,"underline_segments":["Therefore, guinea pigs in Puerto Rico probably came","from Colombia and descended from Colombian guinea pigs."]},{"id":"fe41f258","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Boundaries","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Standard English · Boundaries","passage":"In ancient Greece, an Epicurean was a follower of Epicurus, a philosopher whose beliefs revolved around the pursuit of pleasure. Epicurus defined pleasure as “the absence of pain in the body and of trouble in the ______ that all life’s virtues derived from this absence.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"In ancient Greece, an Epicurean was a follower of Epicurus, a philosopher whose beliefs revolved around the pursuit of pleasure. Epicurus","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"defined pleasure as “the absence of pain in the body and of trouble in the ______ that all life’s virtues derived from this absence.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["soul,” positing","soul”: positing","soul”; positing","soul.” Positing"]},{"id":"7f226b4b","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Boundaries","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Standard English · Boundaries","passage":"In a 2023 study, researchers documented a fascinating behavior in the aquatic plant Elodea densa. When exposed to low levels of light, the — plant’s ______ the cellular organs that generate energy from light reshuffled to form a tightly packed, glass-like surface ideal for collecting more light.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"In a 2023 study, researchers documented a fascinating behavior in the aquatic plant Elodea densa. When exposed to low levels of light, the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"plant’s ______ the cellular organs that generate energy from light—reshuffled to form a tightly packed, glass-like surface ideal for collecting more","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"light.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["chloroplasts","chloroplasts;","chloroplasts,","chloroplasts —"]},{"id":"91fbd59d","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Boundaries","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Standard English · Boundaries","passage":"Award-winning cinematographer James Wong Howe was known for his innovative filming techniques. While filming a boxing match for the movie Body and Soul ______ Howe had a handheld camera operator wear roller skates. This allowed the operator to move smoothly around actors in a boxing ring, creating an immersive experience for viewers.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Award-winning cinematographer James Wong Howe was known for his innovative filming techniques. While filming a boxing match for the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"movie Body and Soul______ Howe had a handheld camera operator wear roller skates. This allowed the operator to move smoothly around actors","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"in a boxing ring, creating an immersive experience for viewers.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["(1947), and","(1947),","(1947) and","(1947)"]},{"id":"36868920","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Boundaries","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Standard English · Boundaries","passage":"Increasing the heat on an uncovered boiling pot of water does not increase the temperature of the water. What increases is the rate at which the water turns to ______ a pressure cooker pot, though, an airtight seal traps the vapor in the pot, creating pressure that allows the temperature of the water to increase past its boiling point.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Increasing the heat on an uncovered boiling pot of water does not increase the temperature of the water. What increases is the rate at which the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"water turns to ______ a pressure cooker pot, though, an airtight seal traps the vapor in the pot, creating pressure that allows the temperature of","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"the water to increase past its boiling point.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["vapor. With","vapor with","vapor, with","vapor and with"]},{"id":"f40b447c","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Standard English · Form, Structure, and Sense","passage":"Featuring jagged peaks of black ink surrounded by hazy swirls of blue and green paint, Zhang Daqian’s 1983 painting Panorama of Mount Lu is ü shanshui, a type of Chinese landscape painting ______ by the use of blue and green hues to depict ethereal, inspired by the tradition of qingl otherworldly landscapes.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Featuring jagged peaks of black ink surrounded by hazy swirls of blue and green paint, Zhang Daqian’s 1983 painting Panorama of Mount Lu is","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"inspired by the tradition of qinglü shanshui, a type of Chinese landscape painting ______ by the use of blue and green hues to depict ethereal,","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"otherworldly landscapes.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["has been characterized","will be characterized","characterized","is characterized"]},{"id":"89ab0d46","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Boundaries","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Standard English · Boundaries","passage":"After the printing press was introduced in 1440, handwritten manuscripts from Europe’s medieval period were often destroyed and the paper used for other purposes. In one instance, pages ______ a collection of Norse tales dating to 1270 were discovered lining a bishop’s miter (hat).","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"After the printing press was introduced in 1440, handwritten manuscripts from Europe’s medieval period were often destroyed and the paper","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"used for other purposes. In one instance, pages ______ a collection of Norse tales dating to 1270 were discovered lining a bishop’s miter (hat).","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["from:","from,","from","from —"]},{"id":"9502ec65","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"When soil becomes contaminated by toxic metals, it can be removed from the ground and disposed of in a landfill. ______ contaminated soil can be detoxified via phytoremediation: plants that can withstand high concentrations of metals absorb the pollutants and store them in their shoots, which are then cut off and safely disposed of, preserving the health of the plants.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"When soil becomes contaminated by toxic metals, it can be removed from the ground and disposed of in a landfill. ______ contaminated soil can","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"be detoxified via phytoremediation: plants that can withstand high concentrations of metals absorb the pollutants and store them in their shoots,","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"which are then cut off and safely disposed of, preserving the health of the plants.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Alternatively,","Specifically,","For example,","As a result,"]},{"id":"b5972710","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"Niger ratified the Outer Space Treaty, an international agreement with over 100 signing nations that acts as the foundation for the laws of space, on February 1, 1967. Jordan, ______ has yet to officially ratify the treaty; it only signed it.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Niger ratified the Outer Space Treaty, an international agreement with over 100 signing nations that acts as the foundation for the laws of space,","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"on February 1, 1967. Jordan, ______ has yet to officially ratify the treaty; it only signed it.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["in contrast,","specifically,","for example,","similarly,"]},{"id":"3c925481","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Expression of Ideas · Rhetorical Synthesis","passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes: Pineapple is a fruit that contains ascorbic acid, an essential nutrient for humans. Every 100 grams (g) of pineapple contains 48 milligrams (mg) of ascorbic acid. Many animals can make ascorbic acid in their bodies, but humans cannot. Humans must get ascorbic acid from foods, including fruits and vegetables. Ascorbic acid is also known as vitamin C. The student wants to provide an example of a fruit that contains vitamin C.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Pineapple is a fruit that contains ascorbic acid, an essential nutrient for humans.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"Every 100 grams (g) of pineapple contains 48 milligrams (mg) of ascorbic acid.","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Many animals can make ascorbic acid in their bodies, but humans cannot.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"Humans must get ascorbic acid from foods, including fruits and vegetables.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"Ascorbic acid is also known as vitamin C.","indent":2}],"question":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Humans cannot make ascorbic acid in their bodies, but they can get it from foods, such as fruits, for example.","Vitamin C, also known as ascorbic acid, can be found in pineapple as well as other fruits.","Since humans cannot make vitamin C in their bodies, they must get it from food.","Many animals can make ascorbic acid, which is also known as vitamin C, in their bodies, but humans cannot."]},{"id":"6e0c60da","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"When one looks at the dark craggy vistas in Hitoshi Fugo’s evocative photo series, one’s mind might wander off to the cratered surfaces of faraway planets. ______ it’s the series’ title, Flying Frying Pan, that brings one back to Earth, reminding the viewer that each photo is actually a close-up view of a familiar household object: a frying pan.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"When one looks at the dark craggy vistas in Hitoshi Fugo’s evocative photo series, one’s mind might wander off to the cratered surfaces of","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"faraway planets. ______ it’s the series’ title, Flying Frying Pan, that brings one back to Earth, reminding the viewer that each photo is actually a","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"close-up view of a familiar household object: a frying pan.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Consequently,","Alternatively,","Ultimately,","Additionally,"]},{"id":"54227b8e","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Expression of Ideas · Rhetorical Synthesis","passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes: The mountain pygmy possum is a mammal species. Up until 1966, it was believed to be extinct. That year, a live mountain pygmy possum was identified in the wild in Australia. The mountain pygmy possum is considered a Lazarus species. “Lazarus species” is a term for living species of organisms that were once believed to be extinct. The student wants to define the term “Lazarus species” and provide an example of one.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"The mountain pygmy possum is a mammal species.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"Up until 1966, it was believed to be extinct.","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"That year, a live mountain pygmy possum was identified in the wild in Australia.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"The mountain pygmy possum is considered a Lazarus species.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"“Lazarus species” is a term for living species of organisms that were once believed to be extinct.","indent":2}],"question":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish these goals?","choices":["The term “Lazarus species” describes a living species of organism, such as the mountain pygmy possum, that was once believed to be extinct.","One example of a Lazarus species is the mountain pygmy possum, a mammal species that was identified in the wild in Australia in 1966.","The mountain pygmy possum, a species of mammal, was identified in the wild in 1966.","Sometimes, a species once believed to be extinct is later found living in the wild."]},{"id":"8622320e","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"Earth’s auroras —colorful displays of light seen above the northern and southern poles — result, broadly speaking, from the Sun’s activity. ______ the Sun releases charged particles that are captured by Earth’s magnetic field and channeled toward the poles. These particles then collide with atoms in the atmosphere, causing the atoms to emit auroral light.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Earth’s auroras—colorful displays of light seen above the northern and southern poles—result, broadly speaking, from the Sun’s activity. ______ the","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Sun releases charged particles that are captured by Earth’s magnetic field and channeled toward the poles. These particles then collide with","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"atoms in the atmosphere, causing the atoms to emit auroral light.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Specifically,","Similarly,","Nevertheless,","Hence,"]}];
